{"schema": "reviewed-by/v1", "decl": "TauCeti.IdealArithmeticFunction.vonMangoldt", "hash": "f48b835ce630", "tauceti": "b3db0f99bffc976c49632ea4690cd96830c4bf3e", "trailer": "Reviewed-by", "by": "CBirkbeck", "kind": "agent", "agent": "Claude Code, Opus 5, session 095781b9", "evidence": "It gives log N(𝔭) exactly when the ideal is 𝔭^k with 𝔭 prime in the monoid of ideals (a nonzero prime ideal) and k ≥ 1, and 0 otherwise, which is the classical ideal von Mangoldt function. The choice in h.choose is harmless because ideal factorisation in 𝓞 K is unique, and the unit ideal gets 0 (vonMangoldt_one). Test mark made while setting up this repository.", "source": {"issue": 2}, "at": "2026-09-21T14:43:34Z"}
